{
  "_about": [
    "How the café is lit through the day. Each keyframe is the look at one time;",
    "everything in between is blended smoothly. Colours are #rrggbb.",
    "sky_top / sky_horizon: the sky at the top of the window and just above the roofs.",
    "outdoor_light: tints the rooftops (#ffffff = full daylight, darker = dimmer).",
    "room_light: tints the room before the lamps add their glow (#ffffff = full daylight).",
    "daylight: extra light falling in through the window, 0 to 1.",
    "lamps: how bright the lamps and candle are, 0 (off) to 1 (fully on).",
    "lit_windows: share of distant windows with a light on, 0 to 1.",
    "stars: how visible the stars and the moon are, 0 to 1.",
    "phases: names for parts of the day, used later by the narrator and the cats.",
    "The keyframes describe a model day whose sun rises at sunrise_looks_like and sets at",
    "sunset_looks_like. The game follows the real sunrise and sunset at latitude/longitude",
    "(Paris) for each date, stretching or squeezing the model day to fit the season.",
    "chosen_times: the look of each time of day you can pick in Settings (Time of day), as a time on the",
    "  model day. The café stays at that look; everything else (drinks cooling, cats coming by) carries on."
  ],
